# Copy this to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values before running
# docker compose up. Lives at <deploy-root>/<environment>/deploy/.env
# on the server — read by docker-compose.yml, and by
# deploy/configure-nginx.sh (over SSH) — nowhere else, deliberately, so
# there's a single source of truth per environment (see
# deploy/configure-nginx.sh's own header for why there's no CLI
# override).

# persona's public landing page domain: solemn.network's domain root
# (a plain A record via GoDaddy, the registrar — an ordinary,
# traditionally-served domain, NOT an EphemNet-delegated apex domain
# the way mera.network is; the two are deliberately kept separate, on
# EphemNet's own recommendation — see P001's 2026-09-30 Log). Deployed
# at the domain root itself, not a subdomain, at the operator's
# explicit direction — persona.solemn.network remains the documented
# longer-term subdomain if/once a separate protocol-spec page is built
# for the root itself.
#   live: solemn.network
#   dev:  (pick a dev-only subdomain once a dev environment is needed)
#
# REAL ISSUE FOUND LIVE 2026-09-30: solemn.network currently resolves
# to THREE A records, not one — 158.174.211.245 (bh2, correct) plus two
# GoDaddy parking/forwarding-page IPs left over from before this domain
# pointed anywhere real. With three round-robin A records, roughly 2/3
# of requests — including Let's Encrypt's own HTTP-01 validator — would
# hit GoDaddy's parking page instead of this server, making certificate
# issuance flaky or fail outright depending on which IP gets picked.
# Remove the two non-bh2 A records in GoDaddy's DNS panel, leaving only
# 158.174.211.245, before running deploy/deploy.sh for the first time.
PERSONA_DOMAIN=

# ---- Second environment (dev), optional ----
#
# Running a second, fully concurrent environment on the *same* Docker
# host needs its own path — <deploy-root>/dev, alongside live's own
# <deploy-root>/live (see deploy/environments.sh) — each with its own
# deploy/.env, and in that second .env, a distinct PERSONA_DOMAIN plus
# non-colliding host ports and a Docker network subnet. Every value
# below defaults to live's own original values if left unset, so
# live's own .env needs none of this.
#
# Live's own defaults, for reference (do NOT copy this line — it's not
# what to paste, see the actual copy-paste block right below it):
#   persona-caddy: 9470 / 9210 — checked LIVE against `bh2` itself on
#   2026-09-30 (not just inferred from docs): cinder occupies
#   9180-9184/9443-9447 (live), 9280-9284/9543-9547 (dev); EphemNet
#   occupies 9190/9450 (live); a fourth product on this server,
#   `offgridapp` (not previously known to this repo's own plan),
#   occupies 9200/9460 (live) — persona's original defaults collided
#   with it before this live check caught it. 9210/9470 is the next
#   free pair as of that check.
#
# COPY-PASTE BLOCK — uncomment and paste exactly as-is below into a
# second environment's own .env (delete the leading "# " from each
# line, change nothing else — no extra spaces, nothing added after the
# number on the same line, or configure-nginx.sh's own strict
# `grep -E '^NAME='` won't match it at all and will silently fall back
# to live's own port instead — see cinder's/EphemNet's own history for
# the real incident this comment exists to prevent):
# PERSONA_CADDY_HTTPS_PORT=9570
# PERSONA_CADDY_HTTP_PORT=9310

# Docker network subnet (must not overlap live's own — see
# deploy/docker-compose.yml's own networks: section for live's default,
# 172.21.1.0/24, corrected 2026-10-01 from an earlier value that was
# accidentally outside RFC 1918's 172.16.0.0/12 private block — see
# that file's own comment). Same copy-paste rule as above:
# PERSONA_EDGE_SUBNET=172.21.2.0/24
